  "description": "CR 613.3 devoid beats an OLDER layer-5 'in addition' effect",
  "note": "Painter's Servant is cast and resolves first, naming blue as it enters (CR 614.1c), so its effect carries that permanent's timestamp (CR 613.7a); the Drone is cast after it, so its timestamp is newer (CR 613.7d). Pure timestamp order would add blue first and apply devoid second, leaving the Drone colourless; CR 613.3 applies the characteristic-defining ability first within layer 5 (devoid is one, CR 702.114a), so the older 'in addition' blue lands on top and the Drone is blue. Blue rather than black, so nothing here is confused with the Drone's printed {B}. The reader, end to end: Red Elemental Blast's 'destroy target blue permanent' mode names the Drone only because it is blue, and it hits the Drone, not the equally blue Servant.",
